{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/648337-quantakinetics-and-the-new-edition","id":648337,"title":"Quantakinetics and the new edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-01T14:18:33-07:00","id":648337,"title":"Quantakinetics and the new edition","content":"The Chitra Bhanu order will be disbanded like in the old edition (i don't expect the setting to change that much) but as survivors or renegades it will be possible to play as a quantakinetic in the new edition? Playing a chib with canon rules would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5811,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","user":"Starkiller","date":". 09-01-2015, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T16:01:27-07:00","id":648438,"title":"","content":"A list of what has been spoiled thus far has been compiled by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill\">Chill</a>, and is quite informative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ayGNCnAsHcgxIUr9k6mNYf46loqY8Qlv5v4TIImqgdU/edit?hl=en&amp;forcehl=1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ayGNCnAsHcgxIUr9k6mNYf46loqY8Qlv5v4TIImqgdU/edit?hl=en&amp;forcehl=1\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ayGNCnAsHcgxIUr9k6mNYf46loqY8Qlv5v4TIImqgdU/edit?hl=en&amp;forcehl=1\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ayGNCnAsHcgxIUr9k6mNYf46loqY8Qlv5v4TIImqgdU/edit?hl=en&amp;forcehl=1 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T16:27:18-07:00","id":648454,"title":"","content":"I believe the QKs will be on the table, eventually, although it might take a bit. As far as I know, there really wasn't ever a system in play for them to begin with aside from a little bitty bit in the Player's Guide and whatever was cooked up in the fan supplement. So, it might wind up being a player's guide/player's option kind of thing instead of right out of the starting gate, or it might be slap dab in the core, hard to say, but we should see it eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T21:40:49-07:00","id":648573,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I would note that <i>India Underground</i>, the quantakinetic sourcebook, was really good for a fan supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T01:35:09-07:00","id":648661,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, i'm kind of pulling for OPP to canonize some bits of Fan supplements, the notion that the Chibs had developed reliable noetic/medical treatment of taint prior to the purge is just a wonderful tragedy and excellent characterization for the Doyen. The Noetics book was another i treated with a degree of canonicity. It would be sloppy indexing to have QK detailed outside of the core Aeon/Psionics book, all the core powers for Psions/proto-psions/psiads/whatever should be found there just for completeness sake, in my humble opinion.<br /> Isn't that what doing away with the meta-plot should yield?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  Vampiric Disciplines are not Aptitude Modes and vice versa 09-02-2015, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T04:41:16-07:00","id":649944,"title":"","content":"Theoretically, although it depends where we start on the timeline. The Chitra Bhanu are already purged as of the very start of Trinity, for instance. So whether that counts as setting or metaplot is a bit up in the air. At that point, it would be easy to have a supplement for &quot;here is QK if you want events where the Chitra Bhanu come back, or for alt timelines where they were never purged, or if a new group develops Quantakinesis.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:05:30-07:00","id":649968,"title":"","content":"Maybe i've misunderstood the purpose of the original Meta-plot a bit, but i thought getting rid of it for this edition would pretty much put all the cards on the table. What if you wanted to play Aeon in the year 2104 or something when the Chibs and Upeo were just like the other orders, will that require another book? It just seems to be the same kind of 'supplement mill' philosophy to leave an aptitude out, splitting up the relevant information into other books further down the line.<br /> -shrug-<br /> Otherwise, i can totally see Quantakinesis being saved for a PG or something - i just thought they were trying to avoid that...<br /> -scratches head-<br /> A supplement of their own seems a bit much, Unless Order/Locale books are being planned, i thought the idea was to publish less, but make it denser and more utilitarian/useful/universal. An optional supplement isn't really something i've heard suggested yet - seems too risky for OPP at this stage of publication.<br /> <br /> Sorry, i'm getting a bit off topic now. But, i'm pretty confident that QK will get an official write-up sometime in the new edition, when is the only issue, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T07:25:29-07:00","id":650092,"title":"","content":"Splitting quantakinesis into another rulebook has as much to do with metaplot as, say, having Gargoyles in the Guide to the Camarilla instead of in the core VTM rulebook. i.e. it has nothing to do with metaplot at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T09:34:31-07:00","id":650247,"title":"","content":"Yes, i think i may have to redefine my understanding of the term. Apologies for the confusion, thanks for setting me straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:19:14-07:00","id":650629,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure setting is whatever is in the main book as first presented, and then metaplot is an in-universe change to that setting presented in a setting, that is is then acknowledged by future supplements while past supplements still remain &quot;canon&quot;, for lack of a better term.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;There were 13 clans of Bungsnappers, but clan Herzegovinia was wiped out centuries ago&quot; is a setting element. &quot;In <i>Time of Poor Decision-Making</i>, clan Herzegovinia is wiped out to nothing when the clan founder is destroyed by the Autocrats during the Week of Poor Stress Management&quot;, is meta-plot. &quot;Clan Runcible has developed the ability to mind control oranges after the founder drank too much radioactive OJ in <i>Rage Across Tropicana</i>&quot; is a meta-plot rules change; &quot;No, you can no longer use Taxidermy in place of Medicine, that was stupid of us&quot; is just a normal rules change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T17:32:56-07:00","id":650755,"title":"","content":"How delightfully colourful. I'll refer to this example in the future if i'm ever confused. Thanks.<br /> -smile-<br /> I still regard placing a single aptitude outside of the core aptitude section to be a bit messy, if QK auxilliaries are still viable and Teleportation is now core material (as i <i>believe</i> is stated in the 'what we know' document), it just seems like QK would belong with the rest. For ease of reference if nothing else.<br /> It's of little matter, just a notion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T21:16:49-07:00","id":650895,"title":"","content":"Aye, for ease of reference I would rather it be in the main book. My only concern is if they don't have time to properly develop it. Also, depending on how psionic powers work, we might see a fair amount of spread over multiple books anyway; the waveform has yet to collapse on this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T00:17:03-07:00","id":650956,"title":"","content":"True, i was imagining the two-three pages required for the way Aptitudes worked in the 1st edition, i have no particular reason to assume they will follow the same conventions. Just trying to improvise with what i have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T07:19:06-07:00","id":651140,"title":"","content":"Quantakinesis needs to be thematically resonant, with Nova powers, otherwise there is really no point to it. It is not unique powerset. It is mirror of quantum one and thus really needs to be that , otherwise it is just bland and pointless. You could give it weirdo properties, to keep it unique, but those are Daredevil powers. Writing it before Abberant books is therefore dangerous and I think a long term mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T06:28:57-07:00","id":652413,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure. In some ways I think if Quantakinesis has more room to toddle off and be it's own thing rather than just being &quot;the psion power that affects nova powers&quot; it might give it more justification for existing in setting. Powers that affect other powers and nothing else always seemed kinda weird and overly meta to me.<br /> <br /> Nova powers, if I'm getting the gist of where things are going, seem to be moving more towards the direction of greater versatility, so it really might be hard to directly tie Quantakinetics to them at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","user":"Wolfgar","date":". 09-05-2015, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:20:36-07:00","id":653053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/648337-quantakinetics-and-the-new-edition?p=651140#post651140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Quantakinesis needs to be thematically resonant, with Nova powers, otherwise there is really no point to it. It is not unique powerset. It is mirror of quantum one and thus really needs to be that , otherwise it is just bland and pointless. You could give it weirdo properties, to keep it unique, but those are Daredevil powers. Writing it before Abberant books is therefore dangerous and I think a long term mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, Aberrant was published 16 years ago, so we have good examples of what nova powers are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T19:11:21-07:00","id":653384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/648337-quantakinetics-and-the-new-edition?p=651140#post651140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Quantakinesis needs to be thematically resonant, with Nova powers, otherwise there is really no point to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. If QuantaK powers have to get covered then let's keep them functionally distinct from and less powerful than anything remotely Nova related, please. I'd argue that if the order remains purged in the revised setting, then let's leave them and their abilities consigned largely to history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T19:47:34-07:00","id":653408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/648337-quantakinetics-and-the-new-edition?p=653384#post653384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. If QuantaK powers have to get covered then let's keep them functionally distinct from and less powerful than anything remotely Nova related, please. I'd argue that if the order remains purged in the revised setting, then let's leave them and their abilities consigned largely to history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded, on both points!<br /> <br /> There's a certain charm to a setting that's willing to say that something is lost and won't be miraculously resurrected. Although I'm not a big fan, think Game of Thrones. They've got the audacity and guts to kill off major players permanently, and leave the world with the scars to prove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","name":"Wintermute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5621_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:41:41-07:00","id":653487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CHILL</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/648337-quantakinetics-and-the-new-edition?p=653384#post653384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. If QuantaK powers have to get covered then let's keep them functionally distinct from and less powerful than anything remotely Nova related, please. I'd argue that if the order remains purged in the revised setting, then let's leave them and their abilities consigned largely to history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Few things ever truly die in science fiction, besides, if you strike Quantakinetics down, they might very well become far more powerful that we can possibly imagine... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T09:29:33-07:00","id":654014,"title":"","content":"I would prefer if the idea of a purge remains that all of the orders are available to be purged. While the influence of the Doyem resulted in the original purge this does not mean that must be the case. The Telepathy order might be subjected to a purge caused by the UN. The Clairsentient order by groups of religious extremists. The Biokinetic order by Law Enforcement (assuming that the &quot;organized crime theme is still a thing). The Vitakinetic order might be attacked by at least socially by the established medical community breaking them as an order and forcing them underground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:05:21-07:00","id":654320,"title":"","content":"I prefer to have them presented so, I can at least have the option.<br /> <br /> For instance, there is a strong possibility of me running three games simultaneously from three of the eras with each one affecting the others. For that Quantakinetics existing might be something that can change over the course of the game, or even back and forth. I might have player have two versions of the same character for the Aeon era game, with one version Quantakinetic and one Psychokinetic, that swap back and forth depending how well players are doing in my Aberrant era game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T08:00:36-07:00","id":656526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/648337-quantakinetics-and-the-new-edition?p=654014#post654014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vitakinetic order might be attacked by at least socially by the established medical community breaking them as an order and forcing them underground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Zweidler remaining in charge of the docs will likely lead to that order's (as we know it) demise. <br /> <br /> You know Proxy Fuego's plan to 'take care' of each order if the need arose? On his entry for the Aesculapians it simply reads &quot;Do nothing, Mathieu will solve this for me&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" c